    content:
      "# POL-01 \u2014 Rules of Engagement (Simulated)\n\n_Simulated training policy for exercise play only. Not real ROE. This platform contains no engagement mechanics._\n\n## 1. Scope\n\nThese rules govern how simulated units respond to contacts and threats within DOIP exercises. The platform simulates **defensive and support operations only**; offensive strike planning is outside scope by design and cannot be scripted.\n\n## 2. Standing rules\n\n1. Observation and reporting are always authorized (SOP-01).\n2. Units hold position and observe on contact; they do not pursue.\n3. Defensive posture changes (SOP-07 Green/Amber/Red) require operator decision, logged with reason.\n4. Escalation beyond posture change \u2014 QRF deployment, airspace closure recommendation, sector lockdown \u2014 requires the role authority defined in REF-04.\n5. No simulated unit acts autonomously against a contact: every response is a human decision, recorded as a decision event.\n\n## 3. Air tracks\n\nCounter-UAS responses follow SOP-05's response ladder and stop at tracking, alerting, and defensive posture. Engagement is not simulated.\n\n## 4. Exercise conduct\n\nRed-Team injects must comply with the fairness constraints in the inject playbook and are always disclosed in the after-action report. Attempting to script actions outside the DSL whitelist is a validation error, not a gray area.",
