    version: "1.0",
    content:
      "# POL-02 \u2014 Data Handling Policy\n\n_Simulated training policy._\n\n## 1. Synthetic-only rule\n\nAll operational data in DOIP is synthetic, generated by the simulation engine or authored as exercise content. It is prohibited to load real operational data \u2014 real unit positions, real personnel records, real sensor feeds, or classified material of any kind \u2014 into any DOIP environment. There is no approved exception path; a system that never contains real data cannot leak it.\n\n## 2. Personnel data\n\nSimulated personnel (names, vitals, rosters) are generated fictions. Real user accounts hold only: username, role, and authentication credentials. User activity (decisions, acknowledgments, annotations) is logged for training review \u2014 participants must be informed that exercise performance is recorded and replayable.\n\n## 3. Retention and replay\n\nEvent logs are append-only and retained for the training program's review period. Runs may be deleted only whole (run-level purge by an admin, itself an audited action) \u2014 selective event deletion is prohibited because it breaks replay integrity.\n\n## 4. Exports\n\nAfter-action reports and analytics exports inherit this policy: synthetic content, role names rather than personal blame framing (POL-03), and the standing disclaimer \u2014 _\u201cTraining & simulation platform. All data is synthetic. Not for operational military use.\u201d_",
