    content:
      "# SOP-02 \u2014 Quick Reaction Force (QRF) Dispatch\n\n_Simulated training document. Not real doctrine._\n\n## 1. Dispatch criteria\n\nQRF dispatch is authorized when any of the following hold: (a) a contact report of severity **high** or **critical** (REF-02); (b) a unit under SOP-06 comms-loss escalation at stage 3; (c) a perimeter alert under SOP-07 confirmed by two independent sensors.\n\n## 2. Authorization\n\nDispatch requires operator action; the system may recommend but never auto-dispatches. The dispatch decision, its timestamp, and the authorizing role are logged as decision events.\n\n## 3. Response standards\n\nQRF acknowledges tasking within 2 sim-minutes and departs within 5. Target time-on-scene is 20 sim-minutes for in-sector responses; cross-sector responses require commander notification. En-route reporting every 5 sim-minutes.\n\n## 4. Feasibility\n\nBefore dispatch, verify: fuel above 30% for the round trip, medical kit aboard for casualty-related calls, and route feasibility under current weather (see SOP-04 route rules). If the primary QRF fails feasibility checks, the escalation matrix (REF-04) designates the alternate.\n\n## 5. Stand-down\n\nQRF returns to ready state only on operator stand-down order, logged with reason.",
