    content:
      "# SOP-03 \u2014 Casualty Evacuation (CASEVAC)\n\n_Simulated training document. Not real doctrine._\n\n## 1. Initiation\n\nA CASEVAC request is initiated when personnel vitals cross critical thresholds (REF-02 medical bands) or a unit transmits a casualty report. The request includes: casualty count, precedence, location, and security status of the pickup site.\n\n## 2. Precedence categories\n\n- **Urgent** \u2014 evacuation within 60 sim-minutes; vitals critical.\n- **Priority** \u2014 within 4 sim-hours; vitals degraded and worsening.\n- **Routine** \u2014 within 24 sim-hours; stable.\n\n## 3. Evacuation chain\n\nCasualties move: point of injury \u2192 casualty collection point \u2192 medical facility. The dispatching operator designates the evacuation asset; UAV assets may relay but never transport. Escort requirements follow SOP-04 when the route crosses an active-threat sector.\n\n## 4. In-transit reporting\n\nThe evacuation asset reports at pickup, at each waypoint, and at handover. Vitals telemetry for the casualty is streamed where equipment allows and attached to the run log.\n\n## 5. Records\n\nEvery CASEVAC generates a timeline entry for the after-action report: request time, dispatch time, pickup time, handover time. The urgent-precedence 60-minute standard is a primary exercise KPI.",
