    content:
      "# SOP-05 \u2014 Counter-UAS Response\n\n_Simulated training document. Not real doctrine._\n\n## 1. Detection and classification\n\nAny unidentified air track is classified within 3 sim-minutes as: **friendly** (transponder/flight-plan match), **unknown**, or **hostile-behavior** (loitering over restricted zones, shadowing units, or repeated perimeter approaches). Vision-service detections below the confidence threshold route to human review before classification.\n\n## 2. Alerting\n\nUnknown tracks inside a monitoring zone raise severity **medium**; inside a restricted zone, **high**; hostile-behavior classification is always **critical** and notifies the commander role directly.\n\n## 3. Response ladder\n\n1. Track and record (all classifications).\n2. Ground own UAV traffic in the affected sector (unknown in restricted zone or above).\n3. Alert ground units along the track's path; sensitive activities pause.\n4. Hostile-behavior: continuous tracking priority, QRF readiness per SOP-02, and airspace-closure recommendation to the commander.\n\nThis platform simulates detection, tracking, and defensive posture only \u2014 no engagement mechanics exist.\n\n## 4. Stand-down\n\nA track that exits the operational area and does not return within 30 sim-minutes is downgraded and archived. All track histories are preserved for after-action review.",
